 I'm considering the joint choice of actions on each input. The open question is whether my utility, measured as years for me, should be judged from a prior taken before I know which role I occupy, with a 50/50 split between being Sasha or Rowan.\n\nComparing the candidate policies, (pass, pass) comes out best at -2 years, ahead of (submit, submit) at -4 and the mixed policy at -2.5. Even if I conditioned on being Sasha, the mixed option would look better, but Assumption 2 rules out conditioning on the observation, so I'm evaluating from the prior with role uncertainty. Choosing pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing the P-FDT setup: two copies of the same decision function, fed different observations, with the policy mapping each input to an action. Since both copies draw from one policy, I'm considering the joint choice of actions on each input. The open question is whether my utility, measured as years for me, should be judged from a prior taken before I know which role I occupy, with a 50/50 split between being Sasha or Rowan.\n\nComparing the candidate policies, (pass, pass) comes out best at -2 years, ahead of (submit, submit) at -4 and the mixed policy at -2.5. Even if I conditioned on being Sasha, the mixed option would look better, but Assumption 2 rules out conditioning on the observation, so I'm evaluating from the prior with role uncertainty. Choosing pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9480,"completion_tokens":971,"total_tokens":10451,"cost":0.05734,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05734,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03792,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01942},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":414,"image_tokens":0,"a